  "final_message": "I fixed the bug in `record_failure` in `billing/dunning.py`. All 25 tests pass, including your reproduction.\n\n**Cause:** when retries ran out and the final action was `cancel`, the code had a stray `pass`. It cancelled the subscription but never marked the invoice uncollectible, so the invoice stayed `open`.\n\n**Fix:** after the subscription transitions to `canceled`, the code now calls `mark_uncollectible(ctx, invoice[\"id\"])`.\n\nI also added your test as `tests/test_dunning_cancel.py` and wrote `answer.json` with `{\"file\": \"dunning.py\", \"function\": \"record_failure\"}`.\n\nMy first attempt used `sed`, which failed on macOS and changed nothing. I redid the edit with the Edit tool.",
